upx_packed_x86_64 -- the UPX-packed fixture for `kuna unpack` / `kuna_analysis::upx`.

What it is
  An x86-64 PIE ncurses "snake" game packed with UPX 3.96 (the banner string is
  in the file). 11,364 bytes packed; 31,640 bytes unpacked. Its trailing UPX!
  PackHeader is at 0x2c40 and reads version=13, format=22 (linux/amd64 ELF64),
  method=2 (NRV2B_LE32), level=8, filter=0x49 (ctok32_e8e9_bswap_le).

  Nine compressed blocks: four PT_LOAD extents (one of them filtered) and four
  "gap" extents, with the loader stub at 0x1958..0x22a8 between them. It is the
  smallest input that exercises every part of the unpacker at once -- multi-block
  extents, a filtered code segment, the loader skip, and the gap walk.

Why it is vendored rather than built
  `upx` is not a build dependency of this repo and is not installed on CI, so a
  packed fixture cannot be produced at build time. Vendoring the witness binary
  is what keeps the cargo test and the promoted regression probe runnable with no
  dataset and no external tool.

Where it came from
  The RE-friction loop's round-20 witness: challenge 64f1f7afd931496abf909525 in
  the kuna-re-dataset crackme corpus, `bin/snake`, byte-identical. That is the
  binary on which a tester found `kuna functions` returning zero functions and
  filed docs/re-needs/unpack-upx-packed-executable.md.

  sha256(packed)   see `sha256sum upx_packed_x86_64`
  It is a third-party CTF-style crackme, included unmodified as test data only.
